+JetPack 7.2 / L4T R39.2.1 build changes captured on 2026-10-03
+===========================================================
+
+Scope and provenance
+--------------------
+This patch captures the local changes used to complete the Edge-AI universal
+build on branch jetpack-7.2-blacksail at:
+  a4acce6fa6d06c047c367bb5f8546583f7434a85
+
+No tracked BSP, BitBake, OE-Core, meta-browser, or other upstream source files
+were edited during the build. The original repositories are clean. This is
+an additive build-workspace patch, not an upstream recipe-fix patch.
+
+The files copied from .build-jetpack-7.2-blacksail are preserved byte for byte.
+Their original locations and SHA256 values are in evidence/captured-files.json.
+The one intentional normalization is in local-build-overrides.conf: its two
+absolute /home/igor/.../host-tools paths become ${TOPDIR}/../../host-tools.
+The exact original configuration block is archived under evidence/.
+
+Three new helpers package operations originally performed manually:
+  replay-host-toolchain.sh: downloads/checks/extracts the two Ubuntu packages
+    and recreates the local GCC support/runtime links and C++20 smoke check.
+  replay-crate-recovery.py: populates missing pinned wasm-tools crates using
+    the alternate official static filename URL and recipe SHA256 values.
+  record-capsule-inputs.py: records the twelve completed capsule/GUID inputs
+    used by final rootfs verification.
+These helpers are packaging glue; they have not been exercised in a complete
+fresh image build. The original image and its verification did pass.
+
+The later review recommendations (bootstrap refactoring, default-pin changes,
+profile-dependency removal, scheduler fixes, persistent cache redesign, etc.)
+were not implemented during the build and are not included in this patch.
+
+Captured changes
+----------------
+* Universal image enablement; 16 task threads, 32 parse threads, make -j16;
+  rm_work; recipe-specific nodejs-native GCC 12 and libcxx-native GCC selection.
+* Narrow browser/runtime, per-module capsule, cleanup, prebuilt capsule, and
+  final release integration configuration files. Scope files unset
+  BBMULTICONFIG before assigning it, clearing inherited append operations.
+* clab-prebuilt-capsules.bbclass: checks 12 capsules and 12 GUID files, replaces
+  completed capsule producer mcdepends with 24 do_install file-checksums.
+  Normal runtime/profile dependencies remain intact. It supports the default
+  twelve-capsule set only, not legacy GUID extensions.
+* Original build/resume/batch runners, runtime package batch, kernel-work
+  cleanup, cache relocation, monitor, detached launcher, and release verifier.
+* Local GCC wrapper, C++20 check source, package checksums, exact revision lock,
+  and archived release/configuration/toolchain evidence.
+
+Not embedded: source clones, downloaded/extracted binary toolchain packages,
+BitBake caches/work trees, images, compiled smoke-test binaries, py-spy binaries,
+logs, sockets, or live process identifiers. Reconstruct the toolchain with the
+helper and let BitBake create the image/caches. Binary packages cannot be
+recreated by a text patch alone.
+
+The evidence/ directory is historical documentation. It deliberately does
+not populate live logs/*.exit, *.cleaned, or build-state.json with old success
+values. Do not copy the archived completed state into an operational workspace.
+
+Host requirements for the captured compiler workaround
+------------------------------------------------------
+The original host was Ubuntu 22.04.5 x86_64, with 32 logical CPUs and 125 GiB
+RAM. The workaround borrows the installed gcc-12, libgcc-12-dev and libstdc++6
+at version 12.3.0-1ubuntu1~22.04.3. The replay helper checks that baseline; it
+does not install system packages or change the host default compiler.
+
+The extracted g++-12 and libstdc++-12-dev packages have the same exact version.
+Their checksums are recorded in host-tools/packages.sha256. If an archive is
+no longer available through APT, supply that exact archive in
+host-tools/packages/; the helper still verifies it before extraction.
+
+The normal Yocto host dependencies, network access, BitBake Unix sockets,
+zstd/tar/debugfs and suitable storage are also required. This build reached
+low disk space despite rm_work because kernels are excluded from rm_work.
+
+Apply and prepare a fresh workspace
+----------------------------------
+Apply this patch at the root of a clean checkout of the base revision above:
+  git apply --check jetpack-7.2-blacksail-build-changes.patch
+  git apply jetpack-7.2-blacksail-build-changes.patch
+
+The package directory itself can act as a new workspace. Alternatively copy
+its contents to a fresh .build-jetpack-7.2-blacksail directory. All helpers
+locate their containing directory, and the metadata expects:
+  <workspace>/tegra-demo-distro/build-edge-ai-nx-16g
+
+From the layer checkout root, prepare the packaged workspace:
+  clab_layer_root=$PWD
+  clab_workspace=$PWD/build-support/jetpack-7.2-blacksail
+  mkdir -p "$clab_workspace/logs"
+  (
+    cd "$clab_workspace"
+    SRC_REV_NVIDIA=8ca9f4a8aa08e46bac501a483b7c4ffb2f3a61c3 \
+    SRC_REV_CLAB=a4acce6fa6d06c047c367bb5f8546583f7434a85 \
+    SRC_REV_BROWSER=886bde2eb0e36ab2b062f563ff0192f9471a1150 \
+    TEGRA_BSP_DIR="$clab_workspace/tegra-demo-distro" \
+      bash -e "$clab_layer_root/tools/run.me" > logs/bootstrap.log 2>&1
+  )
+  bash "$clab_workspace/replay-host-toolchain.sh"
+  (
+    set -e
+    cd "$clab_workspace/tegra-demo-distro"
+    export MACHINE=edge-ai-nx-16g DISTRO=tegrademo
+    source ./compulab-setup-env build-edge-ai-nx-16g
+    printf '\nrequire ${TOPDIR}/../../local-build-overrides.conf\n' >> conf/local.conf
+    bitbake-layers show-appends > "$clab_workspace/logs/show-appends.log" 2>&1
+    bitbake -p > "$clab_workspace/logs/parse.log" 2>&1
+  )
+
+The configuration include above should be added once to a fresh local.conf.
+integration-revisions.json records every selected repository revision.
+The CLAB override is essential: the original bootstrap default selected the
+older d9780f5 revision, not the a4acce6 dependency fix used for this release.
+
+Successful staged build method
+-----------------------------
+Keep clab_workspace set to the absolute workspace path from above. Execute
+the following phases sequentially; proceed only after each command succeeds.
+Do not run multiple runners against this workspace concurrently.
+
+1. Firefox/browser prerequisites, using the runtime-only scope:
+  bash "$clab_workspace/build-batch.sh" \
+    -R "$clab_workspace/batch-configs/browser.conf" mc:edge-ai-runtime:firefox
+  mv "$clab_workspace/logs/build.log" "$clab_workspace/logs/browser-success.log"
+  mv "$clab_workspace/logs/build.exit" "$clab_workspace/logs/browser-success.exit"
+
+2. Twelve capsule variants, grouped by the four modules:
+  bash "$clab_workspace/build-module-batches.sh"
+  python3 "$clab_workspace/record-capsule-inputs.py"
+
+3. Remaining runtime packages:
+  bash "$clab_workspace/build-runtime-packages.sh"
+  mv "$clab_workspace/logs/build.log" "$clab_workspace/logs/runtime-packages.log"
+  mv "$clab_workspace/logs/build.exit" "$clab_workspace/logs/runtime-packages.exit"
+
+4. Shared runtime filesystem, importing the verified completed capsules:
+  bash "$clab_workspace/build-batch.sh" \
+    -R "$clab_workspace/batch-configs/prebuilt-capsules.conf" \
+    mc:edge-ai-runtime:demo-image-weston
+  mv "$clab_workspace/logs/build.log" "$clab_workspace/logs/runtime-image.log"
+  mv "$clab_workspace/logs/build.exit" "$clab_workspace/logs/runtime-image.exit"
+
+5. All four flash profiles and final bundle, retaining their runtime edges:
+  bash "$clab_workspace/build-batch.sh" \
+    -R "$clab_workspace/batch-configs/release-integration.conf" \
+    -c deploy edge-ai-universal-bundle
+  mv "$clab_workspace/logs/build.log" "$clab_workspace/logs/universal-bundle.log"
+  mv "$clab_workspace/logs/build.exit" "$clab_workspace/logs/universal-bundle.exit"
+
+For the original detached-launch method, replace the phase-5 build command
+with the following after phase 4 has produced a fresh runtime-image.exit:
+  printf '{}\n' > "$clab_workspace/build-state.json"
+  python3 "$clab_workspace/launch-release-integration.py"
+Wait for the child to finish and inspect logs/build.exit before archiving its
+log/exit files. Do not start a second runner while that child is active.
+
+6. Verify the exact archive, shared rootfs, profiles, installed capsules,
+   helper syntax/modes and selected runtime packages:
+  python3 "$clab_workspace/verify-release.py"
+The original verifier uses assert and must run without Python optimization
+(no -O and no PYTHONOPTIMIZE). It expects exactly one universal archive in
+the deploy directory. Its receipt does not constitute hardware boot testing.
+
+Stop the idle BitBake server after work completes:
+  (
+    set -e
+    cd "$clab_workspace/tegra-demo-distro"
+    export MACHINE=edge-ai-nx-16g DISTRO=tegrademo
+    source ./compulab-setup-env build-edge-ai-nx-16g
+    bitbake -m
+  )
+
+Manual recovery operations captured by the patch
+-----------------------------------------------
+Fetch: wasm-tools-native was blocked by HTTP 500 for
+wasmtime-internal-jit-debug 36.0.7. The alternate official URL used was:
+  https://static.crates.io/crates/wasmtime-internal-jit-debug/wasmtime-internal-jit-debug-36.0.7.crate
+Its pinned SHA256 is:
+  1287e310fef4c8759a6b5caa0d44eff9a03ebcd6c273729cc39ce3e321a9e26a
+With BitBake idle, replay that recovery with:
+  python3 "$clab_workspace/replay-crate-recovery.py" \
+    --crate wasmtime-internal-jit-debug-36.0.7
+The original operation also populated 36 remaining missing pinned wasm-tools
+crates with this URL form and recipe checksums. Running the helper without
+--crate checks the pinned list and downloads any missing entries. --list-only
+prints that list without network access. No checksum validation is weakened.
+
+Space: the batch runner invokes reclaim-completed-capsule-kernels.sh when
+available workspace space is below 90 GiB. It uses successful per-module exit
+receipts to clean only capsule-config linux-yocto work, preserving sstate and
+separate capsule deploy outputs. completed-capsule-kernels.conf is regenerated;
+the captured file contains the final Nano 4GB cleanup scope.
+
+The original 34 GB download cache was moved to a separate /tmp filesystem,
+retaining the original downloads path as a symlink. The optional captured
+relocate-download-cache.py replays that move and must only run while idle.
+The old absolute destination in evidence/download-cache-location.txt is a
+historical record, not a path to restore. This temporary storage workaround
+is not a durable shared-cache design.
+
+Interruptions: after the original server exited, confirmed orphan parser
+workers and a hash daemon still held inherited locks/sockets. Only those
+identified leftovers were terminated before restart. There is no generic
+kill/delete-lock script in this patch; old process IDs do not identify a new
+build. Prefer the official idle shutdown command above and inspect ownership
+before any manual stale-resource cleanup.
+
+Optional diagnostics: py-spy 0.4.1 was installed in host-tools/diagnostics, but
+host ptrace permissions prevented stack profiling. It is not needed for the
+image. The corresponding binary installation is not embedded in the patch.
+An older download cache was also used to save fetching time; old images or
+sstate were not used as release inputs.
+
+Known limitations retained from the build
+----------------------------------------
+These are the original ad hoc helpers, not the proposed production runner.
+They share/overwrite build.log and build.exit, have no workspace lock, and
+some cleanup/resume decisions trust marker files without input fingerprints.
+The prebuilt class tracks input content but does not prove producer freshness
+against changed source revisions. Regenerate capsules and their receipt after
+changing the integration inputs. The verifier's assertions/path/version
+assumptions and detached launcher's state handling remain as originally used.
+
+The final integration passed 33,949 tasks with 699 warnings, including 675
+automatically recovered deferred-task scheduling warnings. No scheduler or
+SPDX cleanup patch was applied. See evidence/build-report.txt and
+evidence/release-verification.json for the successful image and limitations.
