+++ b/build-support/jetpack-7.2-blacksail/deployment/README.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Deployment fixes captured after the 2026-10-03 flashing failure
+
+The build patch now also records local changes to the extracted NX 16GB
+flashing workspace. These changes were not made to the immutable image
+archive or to tracked BSP sources. See flash-failure-report.txt for evidence,
+validation and the remaining hardware retry.
+
+Captured files:
+- deploy-edge-ai.sh: launcher with scoped temporary UDisks rule and lock.
+- prepare-flash-target.py: exact target guard and pre-GPT unmount checks.
+- clab-flash-target.json: checked board USB serial and NVMe capacity.
+- make-sdcard-automount-fix.patch: delta against original profile make-sdcard.
+- deployment-readiness.snapshot.json: historical state; includes local paths.
+- evidence/device-logs-failed-attempt/: logs saved from the target.
+
+The active fixed launcher remains in .deploy-jetpack-7.2-blacksail/.
+The captured launcher expects deployment-readiness.json beside it. This
+snapshot must not be treated as a fresh hardware verification on another
+host/board. In the checked extraction, prepare-flash-target.py is copied
+as profiles/edge-ai-nx-16g/clab-prepare-flash-target.py with the JSON beside it,
+and the make-sdcard delta has already been applied.
+
+For another extraction of this same image and the same checked board, copy
+the helper and JSON into the NX 16GB profile, and apply the make-sdcard delta
+from the bundle root directory with patch -p1. Place the launcher beside an
+up-to-date readiness file naming that extraction. Recheck EEPROM and USB
+identity before using these files for different hardware.
+
+No permanent automount setting is changed. The launcher rule is installed
+under /run/udev/rules.d only for the checked USB gadget serial, and removed
+on normal exit or a trapped interrupt. Hardware flashing and normal boot
+verification are still pending at capture time.
