+Evidence and likely cause
+- Host failed at partprobe after creating the NVMe GPT at 18:47:53 +0300.
+- Host desktop mounted the old rootfs at 18:47:42 and EFI at 18:47:43.
+- make-sdcard had no unmount check before rewriting GPT and discarded
+  partprobe stderr. Mounted old partitions likely prevented the kernel
+  from rereading the table. The precise partprobe error was not retained.
+- Target export-nvme0n1.log confirms valid GPT, 16 partitions, and the
+  actual 488397168-sector HP SSD EX900 250GB disk. Reported start=0 values
+  mean automatic placement; the target log shows valid nonzero starts.
+- Target bootloader.log and status confirm QSPI commands succeeded.
+  Device-side SUCCESS does not mean that host-side rootfs flashing succeeded.
+- Rootfs copying did not begin. The old NVMe partition layout was replaced,
+  so complete a recovery flash before attempting normal boot.
+- USB disconnect followed the flasher's release/cleanup path; the available
+  evidence does not establish a cable or NVMe hardware fault.
+
+Changes applied to the extracted deployment workspace
+- Launcher installs a temporary UDisks automount rule for this board's
+  exact USB serial, vendor and product. It removes the rule when it exits.
+- Before GPT writes, verify USB ancestry, serial, NVMe export name and
+  capacity, verify the automount guard, unmount target partitions, settle
+  udev, and recheck identity and mounts. Fail before GPT if any check fails.
+- Preserve partprobe stderr. Keep nonzero return fatal; do not ignore it.
+- Record launcher exit status and hold a lock against concurrent flashes.
+- Original archive, kernel/firmware payloads and rootfs were not changed.
+
+Validation and remaining work
+- Bash syntax and launcher ShellCheck passed.
+- Simulated checks passed: old rootfs/EFI unmount, wrong USB rejection,
+  missing guard rejection, and busy unmount rejection before GPT writes.
+- Saved target status, command sequence and five logs in
+  device-logs-failed-attempt/. Hardware retry has not yet been run.
+- Board currently exports the final-status flashpkg, not an APX recovery
+  device. Power off and re-enter force-recovery, then run from repo root:
+  bash .deploy-jetpack-7.2-blacksail/deploy-edge-ai.sh
+  Enter the sudo password in the local terminal.
+- After successful flashing, verify normal boot, SSH, L4T R39.2.1,
+  root filesystem and NVMe partition/mount state.
+
+Upstream script improvements
+- Add pre-GPT target identity and unmount checks to make-sdcard, with a
+  scoped desktop automount guard active for the whole flash session.
+- Retain detailed stderr for partprobe and other partitioning failures.
+- Retrieve device logs even after host storage failure and report host
+  and device status separately; firmware success cannot cover rootfs failure.
+- Replace the detect-only empty numeric SKU test with sequential tests:
+  first check CHECK_BOARDSKU is nonempty, then perform numeric comparison.
+  The line-482 warning was separate from this partitioning failure and the
+  dispatcher independently matched BOARDID=3767 and BOARDSKU=0000.
+
+UDisks rule semantics: UDISKS_IGNORE and UDISKS_AUTO set device hints.
+https://storaged.org/doc/udisks2-api/latest/udisks.8.html
