+
+SUCCESS: JetPack 7.2 / L4T R39.2.1 universal image.
+Branch: jetpack-7.2-blacksail @ a4acce6fa6d06c047c367bb5f8546583f7434a85.
+Final integration: all 33,949 tasks succeeded; no failed tasks.
+Shared image: all 11,581 tasks succeeded, including filesystem/image QA.
+Supports NX 16GB/8GB and Nano 8GB/4GB, with twelve UEFI logo capsules.
+
+Artifact: /home/igor/prj/meta-tegra-compulab/.build-jetpack-7.2-blacksail/tegra-demo-distro/build-edge-ai-nx-16g/tmp/deploy/images/edge-ai-nx-16g/demo-image-weston-edge-ai-universal-6.1+snapshot-f94ae3d6ba49aef86f497998c0e0232a5039510a.tar.zst
+Size: 2069656983 bytes (2.07 GB).
+SHA256: cb1e3e540c3aaec5ff0861b7126611bf80b1f3e09746cb27aedeabe0719c1c2b
+
+Build issues, causes and resolutions
+
+1. Downloads: A crates.io HTTP 500 blocked a pinned wasm-tools dependency.
+   Used its alternate official static URL and verified the recipe SHA256.
+   Other rsync/kernel-cache fetch warnings recovered through retries/mirrors.
+2. Node.js host compiler: GCC 11 lacked the required C++20 constexpr string
+   support. Selected workspace-local GCC 12.3 for nodejs-native; Firefox passed.
+3. Clang/libcxx host linking: An incomplete GCC 12 installation lacked C++
+   development headers/libraries. Added matching workspace files and selected
+   that installation explicitly. GCC/Clang C++20 checks and libcxx passed.
+4. Build configuration: Inherited BBMULTICONFIG appends defeated a narrow
+   override; unset it before assigning scopes. Profiles require the runtime
+   config. A Python integration hook in .conf was rejected and moved to a
+   build-local .bbclass. Original tracked sources remain unchanged.
+5. BitBake scheduling: The large multiconfig graph caused substantial cache
+   scheduling delays. Final integration logged 675 deferred-task deadlocks
+   between configurations; BitBake automatically unblocked every one. Built
+   components separately and reused verified capsule/GUID inputs with 24
+   content checksums. These scheduling warnings remain an upstream issue.
+6. Disk space: rm_work excludes kernels, leaving large completed work trees.
+   Cleaned only completed capsule kernels through BitBake, preserving sstate
+   and capsule outputs. Relocated the 34 GB download cache to /tmp with the
+   original downloads path retained as a symlink.
+7. Execution/recovery: BitBake required approved access to Unix sockets and
+   network outside the sandbox. Interrupted sessions left orphan parsers and
+   a hash daemon holding stale sockets. Process/socket checks proved their
+   identities before cleanup and successful restart. Stack profiling was
+   limited by host permissions; logs and CPU counters supported diagnosis.
+8. Remaining metadata warnings: Old SPDX syntax, absent default S directories
+   in generator-only capsule recipes, and bb.fetch2 deprecation are nonblocking
+   cleanup items. The distro README says R39.2.0; actual pinned code is R39.2.1.
+
+Validation passed: archive SHA256 and decompression; bundled/deployed rootfs
+identity; four SKU checks and shared rootfs links; twelve installed capsule
+hashes matching successful producer outputs; flash/update script syntax;
+Firefox, CUDA and universal runtime packages in the image manifest.
+
+No hardware was flashed or boot-tested.
+Detailed logs and verification evidence are under .build-jetpack-7.2-blacksail/logs.
